  "goodToKnow": "Die Gebärdensprache is sign language. Deutsche Gebärdensprache (DGS) has its own grammar and was officially recognised as a language in 2002. Each country has its own: Austria and Switzerland use different sign languages. Deaf people are gehörlos, and Gebärdendolmetscher interpret on TV and at events. Die Gebärde means gesture. Plural: die Gebärdensprachen."
